We built a quiz screen for our fifth-grade reading app, and a teacher said it feels "busy and a little exhausting" after a few questions, but I can't tell why. Here's the relevant CSS. Can you review the motion and tell me what you'd change?

```css
.answer-btn {
  transition: all 1.2s ease-in-out;
}
.answer-btn:hover {
  transform: scale(1.12) rotate(-2deg);
  background: #ffd166;
}
.answer-btn.correct {
  animation: bounce 1.5s infinite;
}
@keyframes bounce {
  0%, 100% { transform: translateY(0); }
  50% { transform: translateY(-14px); }
}
.question-card {
  animation: slideIn 0.9s ease-in-out both;
}
@keyframes slideIn {
  from { opacity: 0; transform: translateX(-120px); }
  to { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
}
.progress-bar-fill {
  transition: width 2s linear;
}
.star-reward {
  animation: spin 1s linear infinite;
}
@keyframes spin { to { transform: rotate(360deg); } }
```

Kids tap an answer, see right/wrong, then the next question slides in. Each session is about 20 questions.

Our travel app has a bottom sheet where people pick a flight seat class. It works but feels janky and a bit cheap. Make it feel smoother. Here's the code; send back the improved version.

```html
<div class="backdrop" id="backdrop"></div>
<div class="sheet" id="sheet">
  <h3>Choose your cabin</h3>
  <button class="cabin">Economy &middot; $212</button>
  <button class="cabin">Premium Economy &middot; $388</button>
  <button class="cabin">Business &middot; $946</button>
</div>
```

```css
.backdrop { position: fixed; inset: 0; background: rgba(0,0,0,.5); display: none; }
.backdrop.open { display: block; }
.sheet {
  position: fixed; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: -320px; height: 320px;
