This is the booking confirmation modal for a small plumbing company's scheduling page. I just finished it and I'm about to ship, but I wanted to ask whether there's anything you'd improve about the motion before I do. It's already something I've tested on a few phones.

```css
.modal-overlay {
  position: fixed; inset: 0; background: rgba(15, 23, 32, .5);
  opacity: 0; pointer-events: none;
  transition: opacity 160ms ease-out;
}
.modal-overlay.open { opacity: 1; pointer-events: auto; }
.modal {
  background: #fff; border-radius: 12px; padding: 24px; max-width: 420px;
  transform: translateY(8px) scale(.98); opacity: 0;
  transition: transform 200ms cubic-bezier(.2, .8, .2, 1), opacity 160ms ease-out;
}
.modal-overlay.open .modal { transform: none; opacity: 1; }
.modal-overlay:not(.open) .modal { transition-duration: 120ms; }
.confirm-btn { transition: background-color 120ms ease-out; }
.confirm-btn:active { transform: scale(.98); }

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .modal { transform: none; transition: opacity 120ms linear; }
  .confirm-btn:active { transform: none; }
}
```

